Upstream:  https://github.com/juicesharp/rpiv-mono, directory packages/rpiv-ask-user-question
Base:      tag v2.13.8, commit afc21bc25f7d07cae9fb3103dc309240a16b9f49

What came in: the 43 .ts files, under the same relative names. Not copied: locales/, docs/, README.md, package.json, CHANGELOG.md, the tests.

The changes cpd made on top:
(1) Erasable syntax only: the 8 constructor parameter properties (view/components/multi-select-view.ts, view/components/submit-picker.ts, view/components/tab-bar.ts, view/tab-content-strategy.ts) are explicit fields assigned in the constructor.
(2) The i18n imports are gone: the @juicesharp/rpiv-i18n block of index.ts is removed and `t` of state/i18n-bridge.ts is the identity (it returns the fallback).
(3) config.ts reads collapseKey itself, from $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rpiv-ask-user-question/config.json else ~/.config/rpiv-ask-user-question/config.json; the @juicesharp/rpiv-config import and the `guidance` config (GuidanceFields, validateGuidanceFields and their two call sites in ask-user-question.ts) are gone.
(4) limit-text.ts builds the limit sentence and the field note from LIMIT of pi/lib/askguard.ts; the tool description, promptGuidelines and the `question` and `preview` field descriptions (ask-user-question.ts, tool/types.ts) end with them.
(5) The role gate and the stand-down: double-load.ts, and the factory of index.ts registers nothing unless CPD_SESSION is set and CPD_ATTEMPT is not, and stands down while the settings list the npm package.
(6) Comments that cited the removed packages are reworded; no comment cites a record id.
(7) Relative imports end in .ts, not .js (every file that has one), so node runs the copy as the tests import it; one comment of tool/response-envelope.ts is reworded so the import scan of pi/test/ask-user-question/notice.test.ts does not read it as an import.
(8) The tool is registered with exposure "model-only" (pi/ask-user-question/ask-user-question.ts): it is declared to the model but never callable from a codemode script, so pi's codemode mode `only`, which hides every direct tool, keeps it; a script can no longer call tools.ask_user_question.
(9) The mount never hangs: an inline mount wraps the mounted component in a render guard that invalidates it every RENDER_GUARD_TICK_MS (1000 ms), and when its render has not run for RENDER_GUARD_LOST_TICKS (3) consecutive ticks the slot was taken by another dialog (pi's one editor slot) and the mount resolves; every mount, the overlay included, is bounded at MOUNT_BOUND_MS (2 hours). Both resolutions return an error-shaped result (answers: [], cancelled: true) with the new error codes dialog_displaced and dialog_stuck.
